INT. DEPARTMENT OF PAPERWORK - FILE ROOM - DAY

Towering stacks of manila folders. A hum of fluorescents. A sign: "PLEASE TAKE A NUMBER." No one has ever taken a number.

BARNABY OKAFOR-STILLWELL, 40s, junior filing clerk, sits behind a desk stamping forms. His coworker, ODALYS PEREIRA-HOLM, 30s, shuffles a stack. Their cart squeaks.

BARNABY
Form 27B.

ODALYS
Stamped?

BARNABY
Stamped.

ODALYS
Triplicate?

BARNABY
Quadruplicate.

ODALYS
Since when?

BARNABY
Since the memo.

ODALYS
What memo?

BARNABY
The memo that supersedes the memo.

Odalys sighs. The cart rolls away on its own and bumps a shelf. A folder falls. Both stare at it.

BARNABY (CONT'D)
That one's supposed to stay up.

ODALYS
Why?

BARNABY
It's the only copy.

ODALYS
Of what?

BARNABY
Of us.

The door at the end of the aisle swings open. A figure strides in with a clipboard: DIRECTOR PRUDENCE KWAKU-LINDHOLM, 50s, stern, wearing a gray suit and a visitor badge.

DIRECTOR KWAKU
Which of you is Barnaby?

BARNABY
That's me.

DIRECTOR KWAKU
You've been stamping form 27B in triplicate.

BARNABY
Quadruplicate, ma'am.

DIRECTOR KWAKU
It's supposed to be quintuplicate.

ODALYS
Since when?

DIRECTOR KWAKU
Since yesterday.

BARNABY
But the memo said...

DIRECTOR KWAKU
The memo was superseded.

ODALYS
By what?

DIRECTOR KWAKU
By me.

Barnaby looks at Odalys. Odalys looks at the stamp. Director Kwaku makes a small note.

DIRECTOR KWAKU (CONT'D)
Rectify by Friday.

BARNABY
All of them?

DIRECTOR KWAKU
All of them.

ODALYS
That's forty thousand.

DIRECTOR KWAKU
Then you had better start.

She leaves. The door sighs shut. Barnaby slowly lowers the stamp. It makes a small, lonely thud.
